# ==============================================================================
# H.E.M. Associates Portal - Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in your own API keys.
# Do NOT commit `.env.local` to version control.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Supabase (Database & Authentication)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# You can find these in your Supabase Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL: The URL of your Supabase API
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: Public publishable key (sb_publishable_...) or legacy anon key.
# The portal retains this variable name; NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY is not an alias.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY: The secret service role key (keep this secret! used for admin actions)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-publishable-key-here"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key-here"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Maps
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenStreetMap lookup runs through the Supabase google-geocode compatibility route.
# No Google key is needed. Deploy the mapping cache migration and Edge Function.

# Android Firebase configuration belongs in the mobile build.
# FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON and PUSH_WEBHOOK_SECRET belong in Supabase Edge secrets,
# not in the portal or any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable. No AI/Google Maps API key is required.
